  "body": "## What this PR is\n\nThe app wiring for the Rotary Flow operation (#2826). The flow kernel\n(#3630) and the stated-axis rework (#3674) have both merged to `main`;\nthis branch is refreshed against the new `main` and renumbered.\n\nStacked parent #3674 has merged, so the stacking rule is satisfied.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Kind registry: `OpType::RotaryFlow` seats at ordinal 48, digest tag 48.\n  Main appended the waterjet profile (46) and the multi-axis deburr (47)\n  since the wiring was written, so the seat moved.\n- `OpParams::RotaryFlow` with its `ParamsDto` and project-file arms: the\n  picked guide chains' kind, stepover, heights read as ball-center radii\n  about the stated axis, `stated_axis`, `max_tilt_deg`.\n- Project file version **v82**: main took v80 (#3153, minimum cone\n  radius) and v81 (#3674's stated-axis rework), so this PR's Rotary Flow\n  arm renumbered from v80 to v82. `PROJECT_VERSION`, the version pins in\n  `project_roundtrip.rs`, the rotary_stated_axis refusal pin (main's v81\n  form) and the regenerated example all follow.\n- The generate arm: stated-axis flow generation over the picked guide\n  chains, through main's cut-recipe law (`recipe.rs`, no params\n  coordinates).\n- The UI: the Rotary Flow editor on the multiaxis page, its glyph, and\n  the Rotary Flow rows in the op tree.\n- `rotary_letter_gate`: Rotary Flow rides the rotary letter law with its\n  siblings.\n\n## Gate evidence\n\nPrevious round (the branch's own head, recorded on the issue):\n\n```\ncamcraft-motion lib: 624 passed; rotary_flow: 8 passed\ncamcraft-app lib: 307 passed; operations: 125 passed; project_roundtrip: 83 passed\nribbon: 13 passed; rotary_flow_band: 4 passed; rotary_stated_axis: 9 passed;\nrotary_letter: 3 passed; rotary_verify: 10 passed; rotary_parallel_keyway: 1 passed;\nsetup_align_multiaxis: 11 passed; continuous_4axis_part: 10 passed\ncamcraft-ui lib: 1588 passed\nclippy (motion, app, ui, sim, --all-targets, -D warnings): clean\n```\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` per-crate prebuild wedged (#3675): one corrupt\n`boa_engine` artifact, then two out-of-memory link failures (os error\n1455). The suites ran per binary instead, and clippy ran separately.\nWorktree `target/` cleaned after the run.\n\nThis refresh round (after the merge of `origin/main`, on the v82 head):\n\n```\ncamcraft-motion lib: 663 passed; 0 failed; 22 ignored\nrotary_flow: 8 passed; 0 failed; 1 ignored\ncamcraft-app lib: 311 passed; 0 failed\noperations: 125 passed; 6 ignored; project_roundtrip: 84 passed (the v82 round trip)\nribbon: 13 passed; rotary_flow_band: 4 passed; rotary_stated_axis: 11 passed;\nrotary_letter: 3 passed; rotary_verify: 10 passed; rotary_parallel_keyway: 1 passed;\nsetup_align_multiaxis: 11 passed; continuous_4axis_part: 10 passed\ncamcraft-ui lib: 1650 passed; 8 ignored\nclippy (motion, app, ui, --all-targets, -D warnings): clean\n```\n\n## Screenshots\n\nCaptured with the `guide_images.rs` off-screen harness, in a temp\ncapture test on a detached worktree:\n\n- before (base, upstream `main`): the multiaxis editor over the same\n  turned-bar scene, a Rotary Parallel op selected:\n  https://github.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/shots/2826/before-base.png\n  (4x crop: `.../before-editor-4x.png`)\n- after (this head): the Rotary Flow op selected, its glyph in the op\n  tree, the Geometry tab over the picked chain rings:\n  https://github.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/shots/2826/after-rotaryflow.png\n  (4x crop: `.../after-editor-4x.png`)\n- after, the Heights tab: the flow's own rows - the \"Clearance radius\"\n  ball-center cylinder and the Levels group:\n  https://github.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/shots/2826/after-rotaryflow-heights.png\n  (4x crop: `.../after-heights-4x.png`)\n\nPushed to the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch only (house rule, PRs carry\nno PNG commits).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The kernel's swept-ball guard beyond the band fixture (`rotary_flow`\n  test count unchanged) - the kernel PR #3630 owns its own evidence.\n- MCP tooling for the operation: tracked as the follow-up\n  `MCP: <command>` row of the umbrella.\n- Posted G-code goldens for a real machine post - the flow band rides\n  the multiaxis post paths already gated by the sibling rotary tests.\n- A generated flow toolpath in the screenshot scene: the editor, the\n  glyph and the flow's own rows are the PR's visible surface; the\n  generated band itself is pinned by `rotary_flow_band` and the kernel\n  tests.\n\nChangelog: Rotary Flow, a multiaxis flow-line operation over picked guide chains, is wired into the app: parameters, project file (v82), generation, verify, the editor and its glyph.\n\nfork synced at v0.25.0\n\nRefs #2826\n",
